  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the monitoring of progress towards SDG 4 in Southern Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Countries in the Southern Africa region are striving towards the achievement of SDG 4. Indeed, one of the strategic objectives agreed in the SADC Regional Indicative Strategic Development Plan 2020-2030 is to increase &quot;access to quality and relevant education and skills development,&quot; which is fully aligned with SDG 4. Through this activity, UNESCO ROSA will continue to support the Member States in the Southern Africa region in enhancing and strengthening their capacities to collect, analyze and report on relevant data for the monitoring of progress towards SDG 4. The activity also responds to the call made by African states at the Pan African Conference on Education for the joint monitoring and reporting of SDG 4 and the Continental Education Strategy for Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
